{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Error Presentation","role":"article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ErrorPresentation","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Everything the default Error placeholders do beyond showing a generic icon and message: telling a connectivity problem apart from everything else, an optional second action alongside Retry, and a user-facing message distinct from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the one state whose presentation can’t be fully generic — a timed-out request, a missing article, and a malformed response all deserve different words, and sometimes a different action, even though they’re all just an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". This article rounds up the three pieces ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" use to narrow that gap without you writing a fully custom placeholder.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"The offline-aware variant","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-offline-aware-variant"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/isConnectivityError(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" indicating no network connectivity (","type":"text"},{"code":".notConnectedToInternet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".networkConnectionLost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or a timed-out request (","type":"text"},{"code":".timedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). When it’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the default Error placeholders swap their usual warning-triangle icon and “Something Went Wrong” title for a ","type":"text"},{"code":"wifi.exclamationmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" icon and “Connection Issue” instead — the same distinction a fully custom placeholder can make with the same check:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["if ScreenState<Never>.isConnectivityError(error) {","    \/\/ show your own offline-specific treatment","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other error, including other ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" codes, falls back to the generic treatment.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"The secondary action slot","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-secondary-action-slot"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both default Error placeholders take an optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"secondaryAction: (title: String, action: () -> Void)?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alongside ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a second button for something other than retrying, like going back to the previous screen instead of hammering a request that’s going to fail the same way again:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateDefaultErrorView(error: error, onRetry: reload, secondaryAction: (t